0,'Maintenance mode Retry-After header settings','','none'),(9211,'Minimum value for Retry-After header in seconds','','none'),(9212,'Maximum value for Retry-After header in seconds','','none'),(9213,'The MySQL module provides the connection between Drupal and a MySQL, MariaDB or equivalent database. For more information, see the <a href=\":mysql\">online documentation for the MySQL module</a>.','','none'),(9214,'The PostgreSQL module provides the connection between Drupal and a PostgreSQL database. For more information, see the <a href=\":pgsql\">online documentation for the PostgreSQL module</a>.','','none'),(9215,'Deprecated modules found: %module_list.','','none'),(9216,'Deprecated themes found: %theme_list.','','none'),(9217,'Database support for JSON','','none'),(9218,'Non-stable modules','','none'),(9219,'@lifecycle','','11.4.9'),(9220,'View information on the @lifecycle status of the module @module','','11.4.9'),(9221,'Help <span class=\"visually-hidden\">for @module</span>','','11.4.9'),(9222,'Permissions <span class=\"visually-hidden\">for @module</span>','','11.4.9'),(9223,'Configure <span class=\"visually-hidden\">@module</span>','','11.4.9'),(9224,'<a href=\":url\">Deprecated modules</a> are modules that may be removed from the next major release of Drupal core and the relevant contributed module. Use at your own risk.','','none'),(9225,'<a href=\":url\">Deprecated modules</a> are modules that may be removed from the next major release of this project. Use at your own risk.','','none'),(9226,'<a href=\":url\">Deprecated modules</a> are modules that may be removed from the next major release of Drupal core. Use at your own risk.','','none'),(9227,'The @name module is deprecated. (more information)','','none'),(9228,'about the status of the @name module','','none'),(9229,'The following module is experimental: @modules.The following modules are experimental: @modules.','','none'),(9230,'Get the actual @label from a @label revision','','none'),(9231,'Database connection supports the JSON type.','','none'),(9232,'<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/system-requirements\">Database connection does not support JSON.</a>','','none'),(9233,'Media widget','','none'),(9234,'Not all functionality may be available because some information could not be retrieved.','','none'),(9235,'Allow the user to resize images','','none'),(9236,'PostgreSQL has the pg_trgm extension enabled.','','none'),(9237,'The <a href=\":pg_trgm\">pg_trgm</a> PostgreSQL extension is not present. The extension is required by Drupal 10 to improve performance when using PostgreSQL. See <a href=\":requirements\">Drupal database server requirements</a> for more information.','','none'),(9238,'Drupal could not check for the pg_trgm extension: @error.','','none'),(9239,'Alternative text override','','none'),(9240,'Override media image alternative text','','none'),(9241,'Enter media caption','','none'),(9242,'Caption media','','none'),(9243,'Toggle caption off','','none'),(9244,'Toggle caption on','','none'),(9245,'Display help icon to toggle form description','','none'),(9246,'This setting is overridden by the <a href=\":editUrl\">current user</a>. @title: %value','','none'),(9247,'Show a help icon to show/hide form descriptions on content forms.','','none'),(9248,'Back to Administration','','none'),(9249,'Package Manager is a framework for updating Drupal core and installing contributed modules and themes via Composer. It has no user interface, but it provides an API for creating a temporary copy of the current site, making changes to the copy, and then syncing those changes back into the live site.','','none'),(9250,'Package Manager dispatches events before and after various operations, and external code can integrate with it by subscribing to those events. For more information, see <code>package_manager.api.php</code>.','','none'),(9251,'Modules cannot be uninstalled while Package Manager is applying staged changes to the active code base.','','none'),(9252,'Enable form description toggle','','none'),(9253,'Post updating @extension','','none'),(9254,'Press the down arrow key to activate','','none'),(9255,'Decorative image','','none'),(9256,'Add missing alternative text','','none'),(9257,'Change image alternative text','','none'),(9258,'Source editing should only use otherwise unavailable tags and attributes','Validation','none'),(9259,'The following @element_type(s) are already supported by enabled plugins and should not be added to the Source Editing \"Manually editable HTML tags\" field: %overlapping_tags.','','none'),(9260,'The following @element_type(s) are already supported by available plugins and should not be added to the Source Editing \"Manually editable HTML tags\" field. Instead, enable the following plugins to support these @element_types: %overlapping_tags.','','none'),(9261,'There is no staged configuration.','','none'),(9262,'The staged configuration is identical to the active configuration.','','none'),(9263,'The main way to change the overall appearance of your site is to switch the default theme. The core Layout Builder and Layout Discovery modules allow you to define layouts for your site\'s content, and the core Breakpoint module helps themes change appearance for different-sized devices. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','none'),(9264,'Using in-line (quick) settings editing','','none'),(9265,'Edit settings in place.','','none'),(9266,'The core Settings Tray module provides the ability to quickly edit settings inline. It requires the core Contextual Links module in order to expose the links that let you edit in place.','','none'),(9267,'Who can edit settings in place?','','none'),(9268,'In order to follow these steps to edit settings in place, the core Settings Tray module must be installed. Also, either the core Toolbar module or a contributed replacement must be installed. You will need to have <em>Use contextual links</em> permission, as well as permission to edit the particular content or settings.','','none'),(9269,'Find and visit a page on your site that has the settings that you would like to edit.','','none'),(9270,'Click the link to open the contextual links menu, and click <em>Quick edit</em>. An editing form for the settings should appear on the page.','','none'),(9271,'Exposes entities and other resources to other applications using a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Representational_state_transfer\">REST</a> implementation. Data is exchanged using a serialization format such as JSON, and transferred using an authentication method such as HTTP Basic Authentication.','','none'),(9272,'Image loading settings','','none'),(9273,'Loading attribute','','none'),(9274,'Image loading','','none'),(9275,'Lazy render images with native image loading attribute (<em>loading=\"lazy\"</em>). This improves performance by allowing browsers to lazily load images.','','none'),(9276,'Lazy (<em>loading=\"lazy\"</em>)','','none'),(9277,'Eager (<em>loading=\"eager\"</em>)','','none'),(9278,'Image loading attribute','','none'),(9279,'Select the loading attribute for images. <a href=\":link\">Learn more about the loading attribute for images.</a>','','none'),(9280,'Delays loading the image until that section of the page is visible in the browser. When in doubt, lazy loading is recommended.','','none'),(9281,'Force browsers to download an image as soon as possible. This is the browser default for legacy reasons. Only use this option when the image is always expected to render.','','none'),(9282,'Image loading: @attribute','','none'),(9283,'Your PHP installation is too old. Drupal requires at least PHP %version. It is recommended to upgrade to PHP version %recommended or higher for the best ongoing support. See <a href=\"http://php.net/supported-versions.php\">PHP\'s version support documentation</a> and the <a href=\":php_requirements\">Drupal PHP requirements</a> page for more information.','','none'),(9284,'It is recommended to upgrade to PHP version %recommended or higher for the best ongoing support.  See <a href=\"http://php.net/supported-versions.php\">PHP\'s version support documentation</a> and the <a href=\":php_requirements\">Drupal PHP requirements</a> page for more information.','','none'),(9285,'View information on the @lifecycle status of the theme @theme','','none'),(9286,'Drupal multisite is not supported by Package Manager.','','none'),(9287,'Cannot update because the following project version is not in the list of installable releases.Cannot update because the following project versions are not in the list of installable releases.','','none'),(9288,'Xdebug is enabled, which may have a negative performance impact on Package Manager and any modules that use it.','','none'),(9289,'Allow reverse list','','none'),(9290,'Allow start index','','none'),(9291,'Allow the user to reverse an ordered list','','none'),(9292,'Allow the user to specify the start index of an ordered list','','none'),(9293,'Check <a href=\":handbook\">this handbook page</a> for details about compatibility issues of contrib modules.','','none'),(9294,'Source Editing should never allow self-XSS.','Validation','none'),(9295,'The following tag in the Source Editing \"Manually editable HTML tags\" field is a security risk: %dangerous_tag.','','none'),(9296,'@title <span class=\"page-title__language\">(@language translation)</span>','','none'),(9297,'Enabled Alignments','','none'),(9298,'Alignment type','','none'),(9299,'Allow view mode override','','none'),(9300,'These are the alignment types that will appear in the alignment dropdown.','','none'),(9301,'Allow the user to override the default view mode','','none'),(9302,'CKEditor 5 Media plugin in sync with filter settings','Validation','none'),(9303,'The CKEditor 5 \"%cke5_media_plugin_label\" plugin\'s \"%cke5_allow_view_mode_override_label\" setting should be in sync with the \"%filter_media_plugin_label\" filter\'s \"%filter_media_allowed_view_modes_label\" setting: when checked, two or more view modes must be allowed by the filter.','','none'),(9304,'You can choose to send email only if a security update is available, or to be notified about all newer versions. If there are updates available of Drupal core or any of your installed modules and themes, your site will always print a message on the <a href=\":status_report\">status report</a> page. If there is a security update, an error message will be printed on administration pages for users with <a href=\":update_permissions\">permission to view update notifications</a>.','','none'),(9305,'Congratulations and welcome to the Drupal community.','','11.4.9'),(9306,'The %plugin plugin needs another plugin to create <code>@non_creatable_tag</code>, for it to be able to create the following attributes: <code>@attributes_on_tag</code>. Enable a plugin that supports creating this tag. If none exists, you can configure the Source Editing plugin to support it.','','none'),(9307,'Olivero Color Scheme Settings','','none'),(9308,'These settings adjust the look and feel of the Olivero theme. Changing the color below will change the base hue, saturation, and lightness values the Olivero theme uses to determine its internal colors.','','none'),(9309,'Olivero Color Scheme','','none'),(9310,'Derivatives will be formed from this color.','','none'),(9311,'Base Primary Color','','none'),(9312,'@fieldName has changed to @fieldValue','','none'),(9313,'Unable to uninstall the %module module because: @reason.','','none'),(9314,'Unable to install the %theme theme since it requires the %required_module module.','','none'),(9315,'If the <em>Source</em> button is available in the toolbar, users can click this button to disable the visual editor and edit the HTML source directly. After toggling back, the visual editor uses the HTML tags allowed via plugin configuration (and not explicity disallowed by filters) to format the text. Tags not enabled via plugin configuration will be stripped out of the HTML source when the user toggles back to the text editor.','','none'),(9316,'@theme theme','','none'),(9317,'Allowed entity types','','none'),(9318,'Layout density','','none'),(9319,'Hide sidebar panel','','none'),(9320,'Show sidebar panel','','none'),(9321,'Close sidebar panel','','none'),(9322,'Changes the layout density for tables in the admin interface.','','none'),(9323,'The <code>update_fetch_with_http_fallback</code> setting must be disabled.','','none'),(9324,'Resolve all issues below to continue the installation. For help configuring your database server, see the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/installing-drupal\">installation handbook</a>, or contact your hosting provider.','','none'),(9325,'Updating to Drupal @current_major is only supported from Drupal version @required_min_version or higher. If you are trying to update from an older version, first update to the latest version of Drupal @previous_major. (<a href=\":url\">Drupal upgrade guide</a>)','','none'),(9326,'Migrating an Existing Text Format to CKEditor 5','','none'),(9327,'When switching an existing text format to use CKEditor 5, an automatic process is initiated that helps text formats switching to CKEditor 5 from CKEditor 4 (or no text editor) to do so with minimal effort and zero data loss.','','none'),(9328,'This process is designed for there to be no data loss risk in switching to CKEditor 5. However some of your editor\'s functionality may not be 100% equivalent to what was available previously. In most cases, these changes are minimal. After the process completes, status and/or warning messages will summarize any changes that occurred, and more detailed information will be available in the site\'s logs.','','none'),(9329,'CKEditor 5 will attempt to enable plugins that provide equivalent toolbar items to those used prior to switching to CKEditor 5. All core CKEditor 4 plugins and many popular contrib plugins already have CKEditor 5 equivalents. In some cases, functionality that required contrib modules is now built into CKEditor 5. In instances where a plugin does not have an equivalent, no data loss will occur but elements previously provided via the plugin may need to be added manually as HTML via source editing.','','none'),(9330,'Additional migration considerations for text formats with restricted HTML','','none'),(9331,'The “Allowed HTML tags\" field in the “Limit allowed HTML tags and correct Faulty HTML\" filter is now read-only','','none'),(9332,'This field accurately represents the tags/attributes allowed by a text format, but the allowed tags are based on which plugins are enabled and how they are configured. For example, enabling the Underline plugin adds the &lt;u&gt; tag to “Allowed HTML tags\".','','none'),(9333,'The &lt;p&gt; and &lt;br &gt; tags will be automatically added to your text format.','','none'),(9334,'CKEditor 5 requires the &lt;p&gt; and &lt;br &gt; tags to achieve basic functionality. They will be automatically added to “Allowed HTML tags\" on formats that previously did not allow them.','','none'),(9335,'Tags/attributes that are not explicitly supported by any plugin are supported by Source Editing','','none'),(9336,'When a necessary tag/attribute is not directly supported by an available plugin, the \"Source Editing\" plugin is enabled. This plugin is typically used for by passing the CKEditor 5 UI and editing contents as HTML source. In the settings for Source Editing, tags/attributes that aren\'t available via other plugins are added to Source Editing\'s \"Manually editable HTML tags\" setting so they are supported by the text format.','','none'),(9337,'To maintain the capabilities of this text format, <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":ck_migration_url\">the CKEditor 5 migration</a> did the following:','','none'),(9338,'To maintain the capabilities of this text format, the CKEditor 5 migration did the following:','','none'),(9339,'Enabled these plugins: (%plugins).','','none'),(9340,'Added these tags/attributes to the Source Editing Plugin\'s <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":source_edit_url\">Manually editable HTML tags</a> setting: @tag_list','','none'),(9341,'Added these tags/attributes to the Source Editing Plugin\'s Manually editable HTML tags setting: @tag_list','','none'),(9342,'Additional details are available <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":dblog_url\">in your logs</a>.','','none'),(9343,'Additional details are available in your logs.','','none'),(9344,'Updating to CKEditor 5 added support for some previously unsupported tags/attributes.','','none'),(9345,'A plugin introduced support for the following:','','none'),(9346,'for','Ckeditor 5 tag list','none'),(9347,'The @tag tag was added because it is <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":fundamental_tag_link\">required by CKEditor 5</a>.The @tag tags were added because they are <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":fundamental_tag_link\">required by CKEditor 5</a>.','','none'),(9348,'The @tag tag was added because it is required by CKEditor 5.The @tag tags were added because they are required by CKEditor 5.','','none'),(9349,'The tag %tags;The tags %tags;','','none'),(9350,'This attribute: %attributes;These attributes: %attributes;','','none'),(9351,'The migration of %text_format to CKEditor 5 has been saved.','','none'),(9352,'Date range (Datetime range module): Stores time/date periods with a start and an end','','none'),(9353,'Find the view that you would like to edit, and click <em>Edit</em> from the dropdown button. Note that bulk operations work best in a view with a Page display, and a Table format.','','none'),(9354,'Note that anonymous users with this permission are able to edit any content created by any anonymous user.','','none'),(9355,'Note that anonymous users with this permission are able to delete any content created by any anonymous user.','','none'),(9356,'The fallback image style is typically the smallest size image you expect to appear in this space. The fallback image should only appear on a site if an error occurs.','','none'),(9357,'The %relationship_name relationship used in %handler_type %handler is not present in the %display_name display.','','none'),(9358,'Configure @type @current of @total: @item','','none'),(9359,'Heading Level','','none'),(9360,'Updates failed for the entity type %entity_type, for %entity_ids. Check the logs.','','none'),(9361,'Unable to update %entity_type %view due to error @message %function (line %line of %file). <pre>@backtrace_string</pre>','','none'),(9362,'Block content entity changed','Validation','none'),(9363,'Style label','','none'),(9364,'Style tag + classes','','none'),(9365,'A list of classes that will be provided in the \"Style\" dropdown. Enter one or more classes on each line in the format: element.classA.classB|Label. Example: h1.title|Title. Advanced example: h1.fancy.title|Fancy title.<br />These styles should be available in your theme\'s CSS file.','','none'),(9366,'Line @line-number does not contain a valid value. Enter a valid CSS selector containing one or more classes, followed by a pipe symbol and a label.Lines @line-numbers do not contain a valid value. Enter a valid CSS selector containing one or more classes, followed by a pipe symbol and a label.','','none'),(9367,'The following tag is missing the required attribute <code>@required_attribute_name</code>: <code>@provided_element</code>.','','none'),(9368,'The following tag does not have the minimum of @min_attribute_value_count allowed values for the required attribute <code>@required_attribute_name</code>: <code>@provided_element</code>.','','none'),(9369,'Styles can only be specified for already supported tags.','Validation','none'),(9370,'A style can only be specified for an HTML 5 tag. <code>@tag</code> is not an HTML5 tag.','','none'),(9371,'A style must only specify classes not supported by other plugins. The <code>@classes</code> classes on <code>@tag</code> are already supported by the enabled %plugin plugin.','','none'),(9372,'A style must only specify classes not supported by other plugins. The <code>@classes</code> classes on <code>@tag</code> are supported by the %plugin plugin. Remove this style and enable that plugin instead.','','none'),(9373,'Unique label in list','Validation','none'),(9374,'The label %label is not unique.','','none'),(9375,'The Text Editor module provides a framework that other modules (such as <a href=\":ckeditor5\">CKEditor5 module</a>) can use to provide toolbars and other functionality that allow users to format text more easily than typing HTML tags directly. For more information, see the <a href=\":documentation\">online documentation for the Text Editor module</a>.','','none'),(9376,'To search help, you will need to install the core Search module, configure a search page, and add a search block to the Help page or another administrative page. (A search page is provided automatically, and if you use the core Claro administrative theme, a help search block is shown on the main Help page.) Then users with search permissions, and permission to view help, will be able to search help. See the <a href=\":search_help\">Search module help page</a> for more information.','','none'),(9377,'A base theme is a theme that is not meant to be used directly on a site, but instead acts as a scaffolding for building other themes. The core Stable 9 theme is one example; other base themes can be downloaded from the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/project_theme\">Download &amp; Extend page on drupal.org</a>.','','none'),(9378,'The core Filter, Responsive Image, and Path modules provide settings and display options for entities and fields.','','none'),(9379,'A text editor is software (typically, a JavaScript library) that provides buttons and other command mechanisms to make editing HTML text easier. Some editors are called <em>visual</em> or <em>WYSIWYG (What You See Is What You Get)</em> editors; these editors hide the details of HTML from the user, and instead show formatted output on the screen. The core Text Editor module provides a framework for deploying text editors on your site. The core CKEditor 5 module provides CKEditor 5, which is a widely-used JavaScript text editor that creates clean and valid HTML; the module also enforces the HTML tag restrictions in the associated text format. Various contributed modules provide other editors; to install a new editor, besides installing the module, you may need to download the editor library from a third-party site.','','none'),(9380,'Select <em>CKEditor 5</em> as the <em>Text editor</em>, or another text editor that you have installed. The rest of these steps assume you selected <em>CKEditor 5</em>.','','none'),(9381,'Under <em>Toolbar configuration</em>, drag buttons between <em>Available buttons</em> and <em>Active toolbar</em>; only buttons in <em>Active toolbar</em> will be shown to the user. Focusing or hovering over a button will display a tooltip explaining what the button does.','','none'),(9382,'Drag buttons within <em>Active toolbar</em> to the desired order, and group buttons by dragging them between group identifiers; drag <em>a new group identifier</em> to the toolbar to add additional groups.','','none'),(9383,'If you add buttons that require configuration, the <em>CKEditor 5 plugin settings</em> section will be visible, and provide their respective configuration forms.','','none'),(9384,'Click the link for your administrative theme (such as the core Claro theme), near the top of the page, and verify that there is already a search block for help located in the Help region. If not, follow the steps in the related topic to place the <em>Search form</em> block in the Help region. When configuring the block, choose <em>Help</em> as the search page, and in the <em>Pages</em> tab under <em>Visibility</em>, enter <em>/admin/help</em> to make the search form only visible on the main <em>Help</em> page.','','none'),(9385,'Click the shortcut link to add the page to your shortcut list -- in the core Claro administrative theme, the link looks like a star, and is displayed next to the page title. However, if the page is already in your shortcut set, clicking the shortcut link will remove it from your shortcut set.','','none'),(9386,'The Shortcut module creates an add/remove link for each page on your site; the link lets you add or remove the current page from the currently-enabled set of shortcuts (if your theme displays it and you have permission to edit your shortcut set). The core Claro administration theme displays this link next to the page title, as a gray or yellow star. If you click on the gray star, you will add that page to your preferred set of shortcuts. If the page is already part of your shortcut set, the link will be a yellow star, and will allow you to remove the current page from your shortcut set.','','none'),(9387,'Grid - Responsive','','none'),(9388,'Maximum number of columns','','none'),(9389,'Minimum cell width','','none'),(9390,'The maximum number of columns that will be displayed within the grid.','','none'),(9391,'Minimum grid cell width','','none'),(9392,'The minimum width of the grid cells. If the grid container becomes narrow, the grid cells will reflow onto the next row as needed.','','none'),(9393,'Grid gutter spacing','','none'),(9394,'The spacing between the grid cells.','','none'),(9395,'The Drupal application\'s codebase must be writable in order to use Automatic Updates. This includes Drupal core, modules, themes and the Composer dependencies in the <code>vendor</code> directory. This makes Automatic Updates incompatible with some hosting platforms.','','none'),(9396,'Because Package Manager modifies the current site\'s code base, it is intentionally limited in certain ways to prevent unexpected changes to the live site:','','none'),(9397,'It does not support Drupal multi-site installations.','','none'),(9398,'It does not automatically perform version control operations, e.g., with Git. Site administrators are responsible for committing updates.','','none'),(9399,'It can only maintain one copy of the site at any given time. If a copy of the site already exists, another one cannot be created until the existing copy is destroyed.','','none'),(9400,'It associates the temporary copy of the site with the user or session that originally created it, and only that user or session can make changes to it.','','none'),(9401,'It does not allow modules to be uninstalled while syncing changes into live site.','','none'),(9402,'The new package @package will be installed in the directory @path, which already exists but is not managed by Composer.','','none'),(9403,'@message See <a href=\":package-manager-help\">the help page</a> for information on how to resolve the problem.','','none'),(9404,'Staged changes failed to apply, and the site is in an indeterminate state. It is strongly recommended to restore the code and database from a backup.','','none'),(9405,'Post-apply tasks are running in the same request during which staged changes were applied to the active code base. This can result in unpredictable behavior.','','none'),(9406,'Failed to download remote thumbnail file due to \"%error\".','','none'),(9407,'Package Manager is not supported by your environment.','','none'),(9408,'CKEditor 5 plugin settings','','none'),(9409,'Enter a value like \"512\" (bytes), \"80 KB\" (kilobytes) or \"50 MB\" (megabytes) in order to restrict the allowed file size. If left empty the file sizes could be limited only by PHP\'s maximum post and file upload sizes (current limit <strong>%limit</strong>).','','none'),(9410,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@ban_link</em>','','none'),(9411,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@layout_link</em>.','','none'),(9412,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>@export_link</em>.','','none'),(9413,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>Export</em> &gt; <em>@single_export_link</em>.','','none'),(9414,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>Import</em> &gt; <em>@single_import_link</em>.','','none'),(9415,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@contact_link</em>.','','none'),(9416,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@config_link</em>.','','none'),(9417,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@permission_link</em>.','','none'),(9418,'In the <em>Manage</em> administration menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>System</em> &gt; <em>@cron_link</em>. Note the <em>Last run</em> time on the page.','','none'),(9419,'What are security advisories?','','none'),(9420,'A security advisory is a public announcement about a reported security problem in the core software. Contributed projects with a shield icon and \"Stable releases for this project are covered by the security advisory policy\" on their project page are also covered by Drupal\'s security advisory policy. Security advisories are managed by the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/drupal-security-team\">Drupal Security Team</a>.','','none'),(9421,'<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/drupal-security-team/security-advisory-process-and-permissions-policy\">Security advisory process and permissions policy</a>','','none'),(9422,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Content Authoring</em> &gt; <em>@overview_link</em>. The <em>Text editor</em> column in the table shows the text editor that is currently connected to each text format, if any.','','none'),(9423,'Navigate to the page for managing the entity sub-type you want to add the field to. For example, to add a field to a content type, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@content_types_link</em>.','','none'),(9424,'Navigate to the page for managing the entity type you want to add the field to. For example, to add a field to a content type, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@content_types_link</em>.','','none'),(9425,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Content Authoring</em> &gt; <em>@overview_link</em>. If you do not have the core Text Editor module installed, the menu link and page title will instead be <em>Text formats</em>.','','none'),(9426,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>@help_link</em>. Verify that the search block is visible, and try a search.','','none'),(9427,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Media</em> &gt; @styles_link.','','none'),(9428,'Navigate to the page for managing the entity type you want to add the field to. For example, to add a field to a content type, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @content_types_link.','','none'),(9429,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Reports</em> &gt; <em>@translation_updates_link</em>. This report is only available if the core Update Status module is installed.','','none'),(9430,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @media_link.','','none'),(9431,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @content_types_link.','','none'),(9432,'In the <em>Manage</em> administration menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @structure_menu_link.','','none'),(9433,'In the <em>Manage</em> administration menu, navigate <em>Structure</em> &gt; @structure_menu_link.','','none'),(9434,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>@migrate_drupal_upgrade_link</em>.','','none'),(9435,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Media</em> &gt; <em>@styles_link</em>.','','none'),(9436,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Search and Metadata</em> &gt; <em>@search_settings_link</em>.','','none'),(9437,'Source connection','','none'),(9438,'- User defined -','','none'),(9439,'Choose one of the keys from the $databases array or else select \"User defined\" and enter database credentials.','','none'),(9440,'The email address is not made public. It will only be used if you need to be contacted about your account or for opted-in notifications.','','none'),(9441,'Add HTML class','','none'),(9442,'Migration @id did not meet the requirements. @message','','none'),(9443,'Check the <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/en/image.installation.php\">PHP GD installation documentation</a> if you want to add support.','','none'),(9444,'@unsupported<br>@ref','','none'),(9445,'The GD Library for PHP is enabled, but was compiled without support for functions used by the rotate and desaturate effects. It was probably compiled using the official GD libraries from the <a href=\"https://libgd.github.io/\">gdLibrary site</a> instead of the GD library bundled with PHP. You should recompile PHP --with-gd using the bundled GD library. See <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/book.image.php\">the PHP manual</a>.','','none'),(9446,'Supported image file format: %formats.Supported image file formats: %formats.','','none'),(9447,'Unsupported image file format: %formats.Unsupported image file formats: %formats.','','none'),(9448,'No blocks settings to update.','','none'),(9449,'<a href=\":url\">@module</a>','','none'),(9450,'<a href=\":url\">@theme</a>','','none'),(9451,'For more information read the <a href=\":url\">documentation on deprecated modules.</a>','','none'),(9452,'For more information read the <a href=\":url\">documentation on deprecated themes.</a>','','none'),(9453,'You must add the following contributed module and reload this page.You must add the following contributed modules and reload this page.','','none'),(9454,'Removed core moduleRemoved core modules','','none'),(9455,'This module is installed on your site but is no longer provided by Core.These modules are installed on your site but are no longer provided by Core.','','none'),(9456,'You must add the following contributed theme and reload this page.You must add the following contributed themes and reload this page.','','none'),(9457,'Removed core themeRemoved core themes','','none'),(9458,'This theme is installed on your site but is no longer provided by Core.These themes are installed on your site but are no longer provided by Core.','','none'),(9459,'API module providing functionality to stage package installs and updates with Composer.','','none'),(9460,'There is not enough disk space to create a stage directory.','','none'),(9461,'The stage directory has @stage_count instances of @stage_info_file as compared to @active_count in the active directory. This likely indicates that a duplicate extension was installed.','','none'),(9462,'The stage directory has @stage_count instances of @stage_info_file. This likely indicates that a duplicate extension was installed.','','none'),(9463,'The stage root directory will not able to be created at \"@dir\".','','none'),(9464,'The stage root directory \"@dir\" is not writable.','','none'),(9465,'You do not have permission to view @item_label.','','none'),(9466,'Removing media.','','none'),(9467,'These settings apply to the %field field everywhere it is used. Some also impact the way that data is stored and cannot be changed once data has been created.','','none'),(9468,'There is @count entity with @delta or more values in this field,