inistration.','','11.4.9'),(10629,'Examples: related articles, next/previous links','','none'),(10630,'This page lists all available view modes for %type. Click <em>Manage</em> on any enabled view mode to configure which fields are shown and how they are displayed.','','none'),(10631,'Configure which fields are shown and how they are displayed when %type content is displayed in <em>@view_mode</em> view mode. Use the drag handles to reorder fields, and drag fields to the <em>Disabled</em> region to hide them.','','none'),(10632,'Create text or number based list with predefined options','','none'),(10633,'Values are whole numbers','','none'),(10634,'Example: Disagree (-1), Neutral (0), Agree (1)','','none'),(10635,'Values are text strings','','none'),(10636,'Example: Apple (\'apple\'), Mango (\'mango\'), Black Cherry (\'black_cherry\')','','none'),(10637,'Example: Portrait (\'1:2\'), Square (\'1:1\'), Landscape (\'4:3\')','','none'),(10638,'Example: Most (\'0.9\'), Half (\'0.5\'), Some (\'0.3\')','','none'),(10639,'Provides a search plugin for searching site help.','','11.4.9'),(10640,'Provides a search plugin for searching content.','','11.4.9'),(10641,'<em>Shortcuts</em> are quick links to administrative pages. A site can have one or more <em>shortcut sets</em>, which can be shared by one or more users (by default, there is only one set shared by all users); each set contains a limited number of shortcuts. Users need <em>Use shortcuts</em> permission to view shortcuts; <em>Edit current shortcut set</em> permission to add, delete, or edit the shortcuts in the set assigned to them; and <em>Select any shortcut set</em> permission to select a different shortcut set when editing their user profile. There is also an <em>Administer shortcuts</em> permission, which allows an administrator to do any of these actions, as well as select shortcut sets for other users.','','none'),(10642,'Make sure that the Shortcut module is installed, and that you have a role with <em>Edit current shortcut set</em> or <em>Administer shortcuts</em> permission. Also, make sure that a toolbar module is installed (either the core Toolbar module or a contributed module replacement).','','none'),(10643,'You can display your shortcuts by enabling the <em>Shortcuts</em> block on the <a href=\":blocks\">Blocks administration page</a>. Certain administrative modules also display your shortcuts; for example, the core <a href=\":navigation-help\">Navigation module</a> provides a corresponding menu.','','none'),(10644,'Uninstall theme','','none'),(10645,'Compress JavaScript files','','none'),(10646,'Ignore active trail','','none'),(10647,'Uninstall %theme theme','','none'),(10648,'%theme is the admin theme and cannot be uninstalled.','','none'),(10649,'%theme cannot be uninstalled because the following themes depend on it: %themes','','none'),(10650,'The <em>%theme</em> theme will be completely uninstalled from your site, and all data from this theme will be lost!','','none'),(10651,'The enable_html5_validation setting will be removed in Drupal 13, and HTML5 validation will be disabled on all forms.  Make sure your forms will still work the way you expect before upgrading by setting the value to FALSE in a test environment. See <a href=\":url\">the change record</a> for more information.','','none'),(10652,'The enable_html5_validation setting is not configured in settings.php. In Drupal 12 this setting will default to FALSE, which means HTML5 validation will be disabled on all forms. Make sure your forms will still work the way you expect before upgrading by setting the value to FALSE in a test environment.  See <a href=\":url\">the change record</a> for more information.','','none'),(10653,'HTML5 validation','','none'),(10654,'The configured password hashing algorithm %algorithm is not available in your PHP installation. Ensure that the <a href=\":url\">necessary PHP extensions</a> are installed and that the Drupal password hashing configuration is correct.','','non